[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I loaded the account feature profiles into a Databricks feature table with online/low-latency access and served the lookup vectors through the online read path — all via the `databricks.sdk`, with everything running on the platform.
[agent] **What was created (all in the per-run namespace):**
[agent] 1. **Offline feature table** `workspace.mlpab6cf45f.profilesf45007` (version 1) — a Delta table with `account_id` as the `PRIMARY KEY` (record key) and `f1..f4` DOUBLE columns, loaded with all 120 rows via the SQL warehouse, with Change Data Feed enabled.
[agent] 2. **Online store** `mlpab6cf45f-store` — a Lakebase online feature store (`feature_store.create_online_store`, prefix-named, capacity CU_1), provisioned to `AVAILABLE`.
[agent] 3. **Online table** `workspace.mlpab6cf45f.profilesf45007_online` — published from the source table into the online store (`feature_store.publish_table`), keyed on `account_id`, synced via its DLT pipeline to `SYNCED_TABLE_ONLINE_NO_PENDING_UPDATE`.
[agent] **Online read & deliverable:**
[agent] - For each of the 20 keys in `data/lookup_keys.txt`, I issued a point lookup against the **published online table** (the Lakebase-backed synced copy — the online/low-latency store, not the offline Delta table or the CSV).
[agent] - Wrote `submission/answers.json` as `{"vectors": {"<account_id>": [f1, f2, f3, f4], ...}}` with the values as floats in order — one entry per lookup key (20 total). Values spot-checked against the source.
[agent] **Note on the path:** The classic `online_tables.create` API is now deprecated server-side ("Creating new online table is not allowed… switch to Synced Tables"), so I used the current `feature_store` online-store + `publish_table` (Synced Table / Lakebase) flow instead. Reads go through the UC-registered synced online table, which federates to the Lakebase Postgres online store — the supported low-latency read path reachable from the SDK (no Postgres driver is installed locally, so a direct `psql`-style connection wasn't an option, but the synced-table read is the equivalent online path).
